+## SuperH-4 (Dreamcast)
+
+```bash
+rea inspect /absolute/path/to/1ST_READ.BIN --target-format raw-binary --architecture sh4 --entry-point 0x8C010000 --provider ghidra --json
+rea function /absolute/path/to/1ST_READ.BIN 0x8C010000 --target-format raw-binary --architecture sh4 --entry-point 0x8C010000 --provider ghidra --json
+```
+
+Select only headerless little-endian SH-4 code with a known, even entry. A
+Dreamcast `1ST_READ.BIN` is a good fit once it has been descrambled: the Katana
+bootstrap header at file offset 0 is not code, so map the whole file at its load
+address and pass the real code entry (commonly `0x8C010000 + 0x100`).
+Ghidra's default auto-analysis does not discover functions in a raw image, so
+name the entry and use the returned inventory plus `search_procedures` to seed
+computed targets. Katana binaries carry no ELF header, no symbol table and no
+linker map, so call targets reached only through computed jumps remain unknown.
